g isolation, but required-shape and browser transport bounds remain open. Simplification uses the existing contract and canonical snapshot boundary. No new independent adapter P1/P2 was established beyond existing answer/resource ownership. The timer-graph P2 e1ce2d76 persists in the identical validator blob at this head, and root read its unchanged graph loops in the newer a9f3cb53 delivery diff.\n\nTooling/removal: all 18 R100 release moves were fully read and independently verified byte-identical, including four scripts, consumer fixtures/configs, manifest and nine licenses whose recorded hashes match. They are inactive material retaining former root/path assumptions, not successor release support; I6 remains the owner. Root test/gate wiring invokes the active-source check; changed-test selection invokes it when changes exist, with no-change exit preceding it. The lexical check deliberately excludes notes, inactive guides, examples, spikes and CI; it is not exhaustive import resolution, all-component retargeting or outside-duty settlement. Existing CI still references removed room measurement and examples/spikes retain older forms. Those are owned successor work, not a new legacy-build obligation. Measurement tooling names the five active suites; collection runs are not one gate measurement. No comparable full-product tenfold benefit is established.\n\nThe full note contains 150 actual choices; all current common/sibling dispositions remain owed under R1 successor108ea663, R3/R4 and I1. Planner adoption85c18b66 now makes R1 f52573e7 revision10 the authority, without backdating 115–150 adoption. Production authority/read sessions, platform definitions, workspace/tokens/exports, Git publication, provider/device/browser outcomes, complete application/removal and numerical nonentry capacity/resource budgets remain open. Producer 201-case delivery and cost columns describe a smaller substrate, not equal-product cost improvement or final acceptance.\n\nCoverage: client